Draft cells pass, measured in the client with my own sweep: node _harness/sweep_720.mjs fast --only draft,loading --sizes 1920x1080,1280x720 --prefix fw_W5b_ver1_sweep (0 failures). luma.cjs on the 16 cells of fw_W5b_ver1_sweep_1920_draft_myturn.png gives p50 71-98 with at most 3.0 % above 200 (Marund) (_harness/_reports/fw_W5b_ver1_luma_draft_1920.txt). The one exception is Nurrow at 33, whom the UI dims as taken.

Loading cards fail in the client. luma.cjs on my fw_W5b_ver1_sweep_1920_loading_rift.png (_harness/_reports/fw_W5b_ver1_luma_loading_1920.txt):
- whole card p50 34-47;
- plate box (lower 84 %) p50 44-60;
- the criterion asks for p50 70-110.

The art on its own passes. In my own window code (_harness/_reports/fw_W5b_ver1_plates_luma.py / .txt), the 0.714 w/h window at 86 % on all 48 shipped splashes reads p50 76-102 with at most 0.2 % above 200, and the 512 px portraits read p50 71-106 with at most 3.4 %.

The gap is W2's .pcard__art mask (screens.css:417) plus the .pcard__meta scrim, on top of the plate's own baked top-edge darkening. W5b's emulator (_harness/_reports/fw_W5b_card_emu.py, re-run by me) shows the handed-off CSS still misses the gate:
- 'prop' (the handoff): card p50 51-75, median 62; plate region 64-88, median 72;
- 'light': card 55-77; plate 67-89.
So the handoff by itself does not bring the loading cards to p50 >= 70.

Head. art/renders/fighters/rishal/three_rishal.png close cell, next to the concept head crop (_harness/_shots/fw_W5b_ver1_rishal_concept_vs_three.png):
- a white carved face, no longer warm ivory (b* -13.8 on the shipped portrait face, cool);
- a thick pale-blue visor frame (rishal.py:1850 VISOR_RIM 0.0165);
- a nose ridge and a closed mouth;
- the eye recess shows as a dark almond behind the glass.
Portrait zoom: fw_W5b_ver1_rishal_face_zoom.png. The carving is less bold than the concept's, but it is no longer an egg or mannequin face, and it does not read as horror.

Accent. rishal.py:599 REAR_VANES = False. three_qa accent (from the build reports): 2.28 % base, 2.29 % chalkline, 2.28 % lamplit, 100 % in the top half. Lineup art/renders/lineup/rishal_w5b_b1.json: 2.16 / 1.59 / 1.81 / 2.23 % at the four facings, top-half share 1.0, accentOk true. In the game-camera panel (fw_W5b_ver1_rishal_lineup.png) there is no blue mohawk: the crest stands alone and the fins fan to his left. The fins are blue on all three skins' portraits (fw_W5b_ver1_rishal_portraits.png), matching the brief rishal.md:102 and :130.

GLB: 1143 KiB, 20354 tris; three_load_test ok.

My own Blender audit through the heavy queue: heavy.py run -- Blender -b --factory-startup --python art/blender/proto/burdam_audit.py -- --clips cast_ult,victory,dash,idle_lobby --step 1. It read art/.cache/fighters/burdam.blend (15:51, matching the 15:50 GLB); output in _harness/_reports/fw_W5b_ver1_burdam_audit.txt.

